{"name":"Apple Cherry","hex":"#f81404","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common, firm, round fruit produced by a tree of the genus Malus.","The fruit of the tree Malus domestica, chiefly with a green, red, or yellow skin, cultivated in temperate climates for cidermaking, cooking, and eating. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (something) appear like an apple (noun sense 1.1).","To become like an apple.\n\n To collect fir-cones.\n Of a flower bud or vegetable (especially a root vegetable): to grow into the shape of an apple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple"},{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fle